For each fixed x, the map sending a to V(a)(x) is Scott continuous.

Equation (5.14) identifies V(a)(x) with the least fixed point of the step y ↦ x ∪ a(y). The fixed-point operator is Scott continuous in a parameter when the body is Scott continuous in each variable separately. The map a ↦ x ∪ a(y) is Scott continuous because union on the right preserves continuity of application, and each step in y is Scott continuous.
